      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Idle loop (MiniMax H3, same first and last frame)\n\nOne character image becomes a looping idle animation: the clip starts and ends on the input, so it cycles without a seam (\"idle pin\").\n\n**How it works**\n\n- The input is scaled to about 0.6 MP (sides multiples of 32, as H3 needs), BiRefNet cuts the character out, and it is pasted on a flat grey backdrop, which keeps the background still and easy to key.\n- `MiniMaxH3ImageToVideo` gets that image as first and last frame; the prompt asks for small in-place motion and a locked-off camera.\n- 56 frames at 24 fps (H3 lengths are 17k + 5: 39, 56, 73 ...); the last frame repeats the first, so the loop keeps frames 0-54. With another length, set the loop length to length - 1.\n- Outputs: the loop as video, and every loop frame as an RGBA PNG (BiRefNet) for a sprite sheet tool.\n\n**Tips** (r/aigamedev idle-pin recipe): keep one view convention per set (side or three-quarter), keep motion small, key before you quantise, and use one palette per batch.\n\n**Speed:** the 8-step Turbo LoRA from the template runs at 8 steps. For the template's full-step path, bypass it and set 20 steps.\n\n**Models and nodes:** model sets `minimax-h3-i2v`, `utility-tools` (BiRefNet); core nodes only. H3 output falls under the MiniMax H3 Community License.\n"
      ],
      "title": "Read me"
    },
